# 📖 Overview

MultiRole Scheduler Go is a web-based scheduling platform developed using **Go (Golang)**.

The application allows customers to book available schedules online while ensuring that the same schedule cannot be booked by multiple users at the same time.

The system applies **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** with three user roles to provide different permissions for administrators, members, and customers.

This project demonstrates backend development concepts including authentication, authorization, RESTful APIs, database operations, business validation, and secure booking management.

---

# ✨ Features

## 👨‍💼 Admin

- Secure login
- Dashboard overview
- Manage members
- Manage schedules
- View all bookings
- Update booking status
- Delete schedules
- Monitor booking activity

---

## 👤 Member

Members are service providers.

Features:

- Login
- Manage personal schedules
- View booking requests
- Accept bookings
- Reject bookings
- Update availability
- Booking history

---

## 🙋 Customer

Customers can:

- Browse available schedules
- Book online
- View booking status
- Receive booking confirmation
- Track reservation history

---

# 🚫 Schedule Conflict Prevention

One of the core features of this project is preventing double booking.

Before a booking is saved, the backend validates whether the selected schedule is still available.

If another customer has already reserved the same schedule, the request will be rejected.

This validation guarantees data consistency even when multiple users access the application simultaneously.

---

# 🔐 Authentication & Authorization

The application implements secure authentication and authorization.

Features include:

- JWT Authentication
- Protected API Routes
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- Login Validation
- Permission Checking
- Session Authentication

---

# 👥 User Roles

| Role | Permission |
|------|------------|
| Admin | Full system management |
| Member | Manage schedules and bookings |
| Customer | Book available schedules |

